# npm reads this *instead of* .gitignore, so it has to repeat its entries.
node_modules
build
README.md

# The tsconfig carries monorepo-relative paths that resolve only inside this
# checkout, and it has to carry them under this exact name: an IDE's
# TypeScript service reads `tsconfig.json` and nothing else, so a
# `tsconfig.dev.json` beside it is never loaded.
#
# Volto's AddonRegistry reads a published add-on's tsconfig and spreads its
# `paths` over the aliases it has already resolved, so shipping this file
# would rewrite them for the consuming project -- and for whichever unrelated
# package a `paths` entry names. Shipping no tsconfig at all is the safe
# outcome: `getTSConfigPaths` finds no config, and `getAliasesFromTSConfig`
# contributes zero aliases.
tsconfig.json
